From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Afonchenko <undermove@yandex.ru>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 13:40:07 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] Meridian: no H.264 or AAC decoder on Windows either; Windows
 decodes them

As on the Mac: the picture goes to Direct3D 11's decoder and the sound to
Media Foundation's, whose licences Microsoft holds, so this FFmpeg ships
without its own H.264 and AAC decoders there too.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 BUILD.gn                                                 | 7 ++++---
 chromium/config/Chrome/win/arm64/config_components.h     | 4 ++--
 chromium/config/Chrome/win/arm64/libavcodec/codec_list.c | 2 --
 chromium/config/Chrome/win/ia32/config_components.h      | 4 ++--
 chromium/config/Chrome/win/ia32/libavcodec/codec_list.c  | 2 --
 chromium/config/Chrome/win/x64/config_components.h       | 4 ++--
 chromium/config/Chrome/win/x64/libavcodec/codec_list.c   | 2 --
 7 files changed, 10 insertions(+), 15 deletions(-)

diff --git a/BUILD.gn b/BUILD.gn
index f0938e61e1..64b5621bbe 100644
--- a/BUILD.gn
+++ b/BUILD.gn
@@ -4,9 +4,10 @@
 
 import("ffmpeg_generated.gni")
 
-# Meridian: on the Mac, H.264 and AAC are decoded by macOS (VideoToolbox, AudioToolbox), so this
-# FFmpeg ships without its own H.264 and AAC decoders; it keeps their parsers and the MP4 demuxer.
-if (is_mac && ffmpeg_branding == "Chrome") {
+# Meridian: on the Mac and on Windows, H.264 and AAC are decoded by the system (VideoToolbox and
+# AudioToolbox; Direct3D 11 and Media Foundation), whose makers hold the licences. So this FFmpeg
+# ships without its own H.264 and AAC decoders; it keeps their parsers and the MP4 demuxer.
+if ((is_mac || is_win) && ffmpeg_branding == "Chrome") {
   _system_decoded = [
     # H.264
     "*/h264_cabac.c",
diff --git a/chromium/config/Chrome/win/arm64/config_components.h b/chromium/config/Chrome/win/arm64/config_components.h
